# HTTPS in front of Vouch. Caddy gets a certificate for VOUCH_DOMAIN
# automatically when that name points at this machine and port 443 (and 80, for
# the ACME challenge) is reachable, or set up a DNS challenge instead.
#
# Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For to the address it saw and drops any value the
# client sent (it trusts no proxies in front of it), which is what Vouch's
# per-address rate limit relies on. If you put another proxy in front of Caddy,
# configure Caddy's trusted_proxies for it.
{$VOUCH_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy vouch:8770
}
